    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you summarize the main differences between horizontal and vertical scaling for a technical brief? i need to explain it to a stakeholder who isn't a dev, so keep it professional but easy to grasp. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Horizontal scaling, also known as scaling out, involves adding more servers to your infrastructure to distribute the workload across multiple machines. Vertical scaling, or scaling up, refers to upgrading the existing server's hardware, such as adding more CPU or memory, to handle more load. Horizontal scaling is typically more flexible and allows for redundancy, while vertical scaling can lead to a single point of failure and has physical hardware limits.",
      "source": "target",
